rdc","role":"present"}]}],"sources":{},"units":{"CD4503-befale":"Befale territory (Tshuapa province) lies in the central Congo basin, far from the eastern conflict zones, and no armed group is known to hold or operate in it. Befale town, the territory headquarters, is administered by the state with the PNC as the main day-to-day security force. Rural villages of the Befale and Mompono secteurs have thin state presence (scattered police posts) and rely heavily on customary authorities, but no non-state armed actor is reported to exercise control. Web research was unavailable for this run, so confidence is medium for Befale town and low for rural villages."}}